    <div class="prose-block">
        <p>The transition from the warmth of the Greenhouse Council room to the raw edge of the Willamette hillsides is immediate. Your cell stands at the perimeter of the historic wagon-train orchard. To your left, a massive wall of untamed forestry slash sits inside the critical fire-buffer zone. This debris is an open invitation for wildfire come summer, but right now, it is a frozen mass blocking local restoration efforts.</p>
        <p>As you deploy the tool hitches, the temperature plunges. The gray horizon dissolves into a sudden, blinding front of freezing sleet. The wind starts shouting through the historic branches, threatening to coat the ancient bark in a destructive layer of heavy ice. Working as isolated individuals right now would guarantee frostbite, severe gear damage, and total logistical failure.</p>
    </div>

